   "notes": "Headline model OPT-175B is chosen as primary_config, since the paper singles it out; all nine sizes in Table 'Model architecture details' are listed. The text says 'eight Transformer language models', but the table lists nine rows.\n\nThe paper only says the models 'largely follow' GPT-3. That is too vague to inherit specific values, partly because GPT-3 used alternating sparse attention, so no values are marked inherited. The following are left not_stated and should not be filled in from memory:\n- norm type, placement and eps\n- positional encoding\n- d_ff, head_dim and vocab size; the GPT-2 BPE tokenizer is named but its size is not given\n- weight tying\n- which linears carry biases\n\nThe paper says 'All bias terms are initialized as 0', which implies biases exist, but it does not say where. Normalisation ops are omitted from block_ops because the paper never describes them, and the residual adds are shown in their basic form. The metaseq code is cited as the source of truth for details the paper omits."
